  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">220736_EU Sudan Education, Child Protection and School Feeding Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Action aims at supporting children, especially the most vulnerable and marginalized, to access better, safer, and more inclusive education across six States of Sudan. It will rely on four mutually reinforcing pillars, designed to 1) increase girls&apos; and boys&apos; access to quality primary education; 2) ensure that they receive regular nutritious meals on school premises; 3) that they benefit from enhanced child protection services, and 4) form an improved regulatory framework and increased budget allocation to protect and advance children&apos;s rights, however, due to the current political situation in Sudan some of the interventions under pillar four will be postponed to the second and third year of the programme and the implementation will be based on assessing the political situation in Sudan. &amp;#8203;
 
 
 
 Using a holistic, child-rights based approach, the Action will address the key challenges and obstacles preventing children from obtaining quality education, including; 1) issues of accessibility and inclusivity, 2) unequal and inadequate access to livelihood sources that hinders access to children&apos;s consumption of nutritious foods, 3) child protection threats, 4) inadequate policy and budget outlook that puts financial strains on families, and 5) low investment on teachers, that directly affects their level of skills, competencies, and their overall well-being&amp;#8203;</narrative>
  </description>
